# Agent-Facing Content - llms.txt, author-friendly validation, agent audit brief

> Status: **Approved** - owner decisions incorporated. Implementation not
> started yet; the three features are independent and any subset can ship
> first.
> Origin: nimbus (cloudflare/nimbus) review discussion - its three "docs for
> agents / machine-readable corpus" moves: llms.txt exports, pre-build content
> validation with author-friendly errors, and an AGENT.md-style audit brief
> that replaces hardcoded rule checks.

## Why

This hub aggregates content for humans and, increasingly, for AI tools. Three
small, independent features close that gap:

1. **Machine-readable corpus** (`/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt`) - AI tools and
   agents can discover and ingest the hub's aggregated content without
   scraping. Fits the hub's purpose (aggregation) better than a plain site.
2. **Cross-file content validation** the hub's own zod schemas cannot express
   (slug parity across locales, duplicate slugs, missing `index`,
   product-info for unregistered products), with errors that echo the
   offending value and tell the author what to do - nimbus's
   "content-author-friendly errors".
3. **Agent audit brief** in AGENTS.md - how a coding agent audits hub content
   health (validate -> build -> fallback spot-check -> link check), the
   "agent as reviewer" upgrade over hardcoded checks.

## Feature 3a - `/llms.txt` + `/llms-full.txt`

### Format (llmstxt.org convention, as nimbus ships)

- `/llms.txt` - plain-text index: site title + description, then sections
  (Posts, each product's Docs, Products) with `- [Label](url): one-line
  description`. Default-locale URLs; localized URLs listed where natural.
- `/llms-full.txt` - the corpus: full markdown bodies concatenated (posts +
  docs + product-info overviews), one per page, with `# <url>` separators.

### Implementation

- New `src/lib/llms.ts`: shared builders (`buildLlmsIndex(locale)`,
  `buildLlmsFull(locale)`) iterating existing lib helpers
  (`getLocalizedPosts`, per-product docs via `getCollection`, product-info).
- New routes `src/pages/llms.txt.ts` and `src/pages/llms-full.txt.ts`
  (default locale; `Content-Type: text/plain`).
- Raw markdown from `entry.body` (glob loader exposes it); `withBase()` for
  URLs so a sub-path deploy still works.
- Decision 1 (resolved): default-locale only. No `/[locale]/llms.txt`
  variants in v1.

### Files touched (3a)

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/lib/llms.ts` | **new** - index + full builders |
| `src/pages/llms.txt.ts` | **new** - GET route |
| `src/pages/llms-full.txt.ts` | **new** - GET route |
| `src/pages/robots.txt.ts` | optional: reference llms.txt |
| `README.md` | optional: mention the endpoints |

## Feature 3b - cross-file content validation (`validate:content`)

### What zod cannot check today (error vs warning per owner decision 3)

**Errors** (would break or corrupt the build - exit non-zero):

- Duplicate slugs within one locale, including nested-dir collisions
  (`foo.md` vs `foo/index.md` resolve to the same route; Astro fails the
  build - a friendly pre-check catches it earlier with both files named).

**Warnings** (do not affect the build - reported, still exit 0):

- Slug parity: a `zh-Hans`-only slug with no `en` counterpart breaks fallback
  (the en route is simply absent; the build still passes).
- Missing `index.md` for a product+locale: the docs landing page is silently
  absent. `en` missing is serious (no docs home at all) but still builds;
  `zh` missing is the normal fallback case.
- `product-info/<locale>/<slug>.md` for a slug not in `products`: renders
  nothing.
- Drafts excluded (informational); `landing/`-style checks on the hub side.

### Approach

- New stdlib-only script `skills/site-content/scripts/validate-hub-content.mjs`
  (no deps, matching the examples' validator ethos) that walks
  `src/content/` and reports, per issue: `file -> field -> offending value ->
  fix hint`. Lives with the content-authoring skill because it is the
  pre-commit gate for content providers (owner decision 4).
- Error vs warning (owner decision 3): issues that would fail the build are
  **errors** (exit non-zero); issues that do not affect the build are
  **warnings** (reported, still exit 0).
- `package.json`: `"validate:content": "node scripts/validate-hub-content.mjs"`.
- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`: run it as a step before `npm run build`.
- `skills/site-content/SKILL.md` + AGENTS.md: document the command as the
  pre-commit gate for authors.
- Errors borrow nimbus's style: echo the offending value, name the file, say
  exactly what to change.

### Files touched (3b)

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `skills/site-content/scripts/validate-hub-content.mjs` | **new** - the content-provider gate; lives with the authoring skill (decision 4) |
| `package.json` | `validate:content` script |
| `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` | validation step before build |
| `skills/site-content/SKILL.md` | document the gate |
| `AGENTS.md` | mention in the verification section |

## Feature 3c - agent audit brief (AGENTS.md)

A short "Content health audit" section telling a coding agent how to verify
the hub end to end before claiming done:

1. `npm run validate:content` - cross-file rules.
2. `npm run build` - zod types + routes + broken links.
3. Spot-check `dist/` - a fallback page (`/zh-Hans/...` renders the en body
   with a notice), `lang`/hreflang correctness, `llms.txt` presence.
4. (If touching the sync skill) `npm run check:examples` (plan: examples
   consistency).

This replaces ad-hoc "run the build" instructions with a repeatable brief -
the nimbus AGENT.md idea, folded into our existing AGENTS.md (we already have
the file; no new root doc needed).

### Files touched (3c)

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | new "Verifying content health (agent audit brief)" section |

## Decisions (resolved, owner review)

1. **llms.txt: default-locale only.** No `/[locale]/llms.txt` variants.
2. **llms-full includes product-info** (corpus = posts + docs +
   product-info bodies).
3. **Warning unless it breaks the build.** Errors = things that fail/corrupt
   the build (duplicate slugs); everything else (slug parity, missing
   `index.md`, product-info for unknown products) = warnings, reported but
   exit 0.
4. **Validator lives in `skills/site-content/scripts/`** - it is the
   pre-commit gate for content providers, the skill's audience.

## Implementation order

1. Feature 3a (llms) - lib + 2 routes; build + curl check.
2. Feature 3b (validator) - `skills/site-content/scripts/` script + npm
   script + CI step.
3. Feature 3c (audit brief) - AGENTS.md section.

Each is an independent commit; any subset can ship.

## Verification checklist

- `npm run build` passes; `dist/llms.txt` and `dist/llms-full.txt` exist and
  contain the expected sections.
- `npm run validate:content` passes on the current tree (0 errors; any
  existing quality nits surface as warnings, exit 0).
- Introducing a duplicate slug makes it fail (error) with a value-echoing
  message naming both files; introducing a `zh-Hans`-only slug surfaces a
  warning only.
- A fallback page still renders with the notice (unchanged behavior).
- `robots.txt` (if changed) is still valid.

## Out of scope

- Feeding the corpus to an LLM/RAG pipeline (endpoints only).
- Per-locale llms.txt variants (deferred).
- Real remark/rehype plugins for validation (the content pass is
  stdlib-based, no new dependencies - per AGENTS.md, no dependency installs
  without authorization).
